# Samurai Linux APT pinning.
#
# Every archive Samurai Linux installs from is one of Debian's, fetched over
# http and authenticated by Release-file signature against
# /usr/share/keyrings/debian-archive-keyring.gpg; no third-party repository is
# configured. .deb files are not GPG-checked individually - Debian does not sign
# them - which is why 0120-security.hook.chroot insists the security pocket is
# present and verifiable at build time.
#
# Pinning decides which of them wins when the same package exists in more than
# one, so a mirror lagging behind the security archive can never leave a patched
# package unupgraded, and no test or debug pocket of the archive can be pulled in
# by accident.
#
# Priority semantics (apt_preferences(5)):
#   600 - security: always preferred, may step a package down to a patched
#         older version rather than leave a CVE unserved
#   500 - the normal release and its update pocket
#     1 - everything else in Debian, installable only with an explicit -t

Package: *
Pin: release n=trixie-security
Pin-Priority: 600

Package: *
Pin: release n=trixie
Pin-Priority: 500

Package: *
Pin: release n=trixie-updates
Pin-Priority: 500

Package: *
Pin: release n=trixie-backports
Pin-Priority: 1

Package: *
Pin: release n=trixie-proposed-updates
Pin-Priority: 1
